 "about": "Both hands close on the Earth (`earth`, an actor about half a metre across) slowly, fingers soft and spread, the eyes on it, lips pressed; a held beat of care; then the hands let go (`let`) and come up open at the chest, okay okay, a step back in the hips, a relieved breath and a small smile. The Earth going back to its place is the card's, after `let`. Works for both of them. No ground. Ends hands up. Plays `base` (IdleBreathe) under it from the start, so the take has a clip of its own and nothing adds up when it is baked or played alone (base 0 leaves what plays underneath).",
